<title>USA: Silicon Storage asks to join Sanyo in probe.</title>
<headline>Silicon Storage asks to join Sanyo in probe.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Silicon Storage Technology Inc said that it has petitioned the International Trade Commission (ITC) to become a party to its investigation of a complaint filed by Atmel Corp alleging patent infringement by Sanyo Electric Co Ltd and Winbond Electronics Corp of Taiwan.</p>
<p>In a statement released late on Friday, Silicon said that it was sued by Atmel in January 1996 for alleged patent infringement. Silicon filed a counterclaim in February 1996.</p>
<p>Silicon said that briefs were filed in opposition to Atmel's motions for summary judgement in February 1997.</p>
</text>
